From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:43:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 441/443] wifi: mt6797: ignore a scan-done event nothing waits
 for

Right after the first scan with probe requests, a second done event
reached the join worker, which refused it as unknown and ended the
lifetime with -EPROTO. Ignore it: the scan it could belong to is over.

Part of the Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 3.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c
index e83221d17..bbf4b95f4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join.c
@@ -1029,10 +1029,10 @@ static int mt6797_mac_join_control_event(struct mt6797_mac *mac, size_t bytes)
 	/* Same bounded notifications as the proven scan consumer; no body log. */
 	if (mac->join_packet[4] == 0x27)
 		return 0;
-	/* EVENT_ID_SCAN_DONE; one from a scan just cancelled is not owed. */
+	/* EVENT_ID_SCAN_DONE. One that nothing waits for is not a fault: a scan
+	 * just cancelled, or the extra one that follows a scan with probes.
+	 */
 	if (mac->join_packet[4] == 0x0d) {
-		if (!mac->join_data_phase)
-			return -EPROTO;
 		mt6797_mac_online_scan_done(mac, bytes);
 		return 0;
 	}
